- "Problem is with our current cups is he’s stopped trying to practice drinking and only wants to pull the straw out. The Honey Bear cup was so easy to get out there’s no ring blocked thingy whatsoever. And the Lalo cup has a small ring stopper but he’s strong and figured it out after awhile. I put 1 elastic around the straw and he still pulled the straw through. I put 2 and he ended up pulling the lid out with the straw and spilling water everywhere." [sr027-0167]
- "We started with pre-walkers so the very soft almost sock like ones which she found most confusing. Now she has shoes with a harder sole which work a little bit better actually but she still tries to get them off." [sr002-0248]
- "She’s torn the corner guards off of everything (we’ve gotten rid of our coffee table, but still have a TV console..)" [sr008-0004]
- "For this bath we took the seat out and I tried holding her. I had to get in with her and even then she was fighting me to sit by herself even though she cant yet lol." [sr070-0078]
- "Adding that we used to use sleep sacks, but he knows how to unzip them (also tried putting it on backwards)." [sr070-0116]
- "Currently I have a nice setup for their toys - open-ended, toy rotation, all in full view. I've bought a small laundry basket for them, a bookshelf, and I'm looking into a set of wooden utensils for cutting bananas etc." [sr068-0043]
- "We practice with a tiny open cup at meals, which mostly means she gets one sip and the high-chair tray gets the rest. I don’t mind a little mess, but I’d love something she can hold herself while she is learning." [sr098-0134]
- "Oh good to know they looked smaller! He has some play blocks from Fat Brain Toys I had to hide some of because he could fit the whole block in his mouth (despite it saying 12+ months)" [sr121-0090]
- "We've had her stay on a floor bed at grandma's house for an overnight visit, but we put a play pen fence around the mattress area in case she decided to run. She didn't, and handled the night like a champ." [sr128-0127]

### What other people told them or did

- "So my 10 month old little one is walking and his grands are constantly pressuring me about him wearing the old fashioned walking booties even though he walks best barefoot. The booties are flat, offer no support, and causes him to struggle a lot when he’s trying to get across a room." [sr002-0168]
- "my coworker said I need to start putting him in shoes or else he will get flat feet?" [sr049-0049]
- "I’m prefacing by saying that I know shoes aren’t recommended until they can walk. And I had zero intentions on putting her in shoes anytime soon before today. But daycare said they need shoes once they start pulling up. Yay. So I’m looking to see what I can find that is appropriate for her age. Thanks!!" [sr060-0040]
- "I been getting ads for Lovevery, Kiwico and some others." [sr034-0057]
- "My grandma is insisting she gets us a play pen. We already have a pack n play that we dont use, but keep for if we need it if we stay the night somewhere." [sr046-0109]
- "Our baby is 10 months right now but my sister said I should start making a registry for his first birthday. We'll take anything, but to avoid just getting a million toys and outfits im looking for actual useful things that he won't throw or outgrow in 2 minutes." [sr087-0067]
- "Do you have the full size or the mini/travel Yoto? My 3 year old nephew is still hit or miss on their Yoto which is why I was wondering if we needed to wait" [sr121-0086]
- "We have been kindly gifted a £100 John Lewis voucher for our baby." [sr115-0022]
- "Hello! My baby is turning 1 soon and my in-laws are asking for birthday ideas! The problem is, I’m stumped because this is our second child (and the same gender as our first) and I feel like we already have everything we need!" [sr025-0025]
- "I was using the infintino but I heard it’s not good to have there legs dangling." [sr052-0118]

### What they bought or paid for

- "I got this box of Lego at a flea market today for $40." [sr012-0123]
- "Then we gotLalo silicone cup that we can also fairly easily squirt water in his mouth but he wasn’t able to do so." [sr027-0165]
- "I've bought a small laundry basket for them, a bookshelf, and I'm looking into a set of wooden utensils for cutting bananas etc." [sr068-0043]
- "☆shoes (we buy them ourselves to insure proper fit)" [sr105-0045]
- "Boppy nursing pillows - I bought two of these because I used it so much for my first born, but they changed the shape and it was horrible! I’ve been using regular pillows. I can’t speak to the rest of the nursing pillows, but Boppy is not the way to go." [sr118-0049]
- "I definitely got the pumps with the intention of pumping at work, but life happened and I actually had to quit working." [sr118-0065]
- "I got mine off of Amazon, I really like them and they are super comfortable and just all around more supportive." [sr118-0074]
- "i need toy recommendations that wont require me to keep buying toys he doesn’t touch :)" [sr002-0032]
- "What suggestions or recommendations do you guys have? So far I've tried a few different sizes of FeetCity mesh shoes I've found on Amazon and have a pair of Tiny Explorings sock shoes on the way." [sr022-0111]

### How they say they feel

- "My daughter is 7 months old and I am just realizing Easter is tomorrow... does she need an Easter basket, am I gonna feel guilty if I don't get her one? what do I even put in a 7 month olds Easter basket 😂😂 help?" [sr001-0126]
- "there’s so much and I feel overwhelmed lol" [sr008-0004]
- "my baby is finally getting a nursery (I am ecstatic lol)" [sr009-0056]
- "We used Nuk sippies to transition her from the bottle and are still using them but I HATE them." [sr049-0016]
- "Any advice? I'm so so sick of this and ready to move on with my life." [sr069-0016]
- "I'm a proud mum of twin girls, 16 months old." [sr068-0042]
- "Feeling very confused with all the recommendations and options - advice would be greatly appreciated!!" [sr070-0041]
- "As first time mom I am very concerned what my baby takes in mouth I don’t want my baby to gulp something as being baby their digestive system is still developing." [sr080-0058]
- "Breaks my heart a little bit each time I see it." [sr081-0092]
- "I’m excited to introduce my son to Star wars, however, he’s only 3 weeks." [sr097-0010]
- "I  wanted to look for something long-term and I am getting very overwhelmed." [sr100-0007]
- "But I dont want to move her too soon and I also worry about her running around her room at night." [sr128-0127]


