### They question whether buying another toy is useful at this age.

5 of 123 posts.

Parents ask whether a play kitchen or magnetic tiles will produce play or scattered clutter, and whether an older-age-labelled toy brings hazards or frustration. One parent compares a sixteen-month-old's supply with social-media playrooms, while another says a cheap water bottle beats fancy toys. Other posts concern an almost-two-year-old, an eighteen-month-old and a baby enjoying an eighteen-month-plus toy.

- "My question is at her age, do toddlers just take all the items off and run around the home with it? I don't want to constantly be putting it back together every day and putting clutter away." [sr019-0022]
