### They want feeding equipment that fits the child, enables drinking or eating, and is manageable to use.

9 of 123 posts.

Parents ask about cups, bottle handles, milk transitions, supportive highchairs and toddler seating from about five to eighteen months. Obstacles include small hands, thighs that do not fit an insert, unsupported feet, a baby climbing out, many tiny cup parts, and a highchair so hard to clean that it discourages self-led meals. Budget, allergies and a tiny kitchen can narrow the options as much as age does.

