### They want a seat or support that works before or after independent sitting.

7 of 123 posts.

These requests concern floor seats, activity centres, bouncers and bath supports from thirteen weeks to seven months. Some children want to be upright but still need support; others have learned to sit or kick and no longer suit a bath lounger or insert. Large size can bring a weight limit before the parent expects, and parents also ask about restricted movement, container time and washing a wet baby's bottom.

- "Is it too early to get her some kind of seat for support?" [sr042-0002]
- "She currently can sit upright with support, so something that can help prop her up while also not restricting her movements would be ideal. She’s in it at most 15-20 minutes once a day and ideally it would be a chair I can place directly on the floor. Thank you!" [sr069-0077]
- "My baby is just about to turn 6mo old, which I've heard is the earliest you should put them in one of those, but he's already about 25lbs and that seems to be the weight limit on most things I've seen!" [sr030-0016]
- "So our little one is  almost 3 months old and weighing a whopping 19lbs😅 hes taking the 97th percentile thing seriously.. he recently started to love his bouncer chair but it only goes up to 20lbs" [sr129-0084]
- "I’ve got the angelcare bath insert and little miss has discovered a joy of thrashing her legs up and down, to the point she’s going to trash herself right out of the the thing and into the bath at large. Obviously not ideal to allow her to begin her free diving career before she can even independently sit, so does anyone have any recommendations (\*or warnings\*) for any of the other baths out there?" [sr072-0040]
- "Hey everyone I have a 7 month old girl who loves the bath and loves to sit up! She is sitting independently now and her bath “ lounger “ just seems uncomfortable for her now and I’m looking into getting her one of those bath seats. I have a weird question though.. how do you get their bottom cleaned when they’re sitting like that in the bath? She’s like 20 lbs so I’m not sure I can safely hold her up with one hand and wash with the other especially while she’s wet. Is there another product that is better for this age range ?" [sr119-0036]

