### They want open-ended toys for active or imaginative play.

4 of 123 posts.

These posts ask for toys that the child engages with, rather than toys that supply lights and songs. They include first-birthday plans, ten-month-olds' current toys, rotation, and materials that will last. One parent wants wooden quality without ruling out plastic and is searching for secondhand kits because the preferred brand is expensive.

- "I’m starting to plan my daughter’s first birthday and putting together a registry with toys and activities she can grow into. We’re focusing on affordable, open-ended toys that encourage creativity and independent play—no light-up or battery-operated toys for now." [sr003-0197]
- "What non light up singing toys does your 10 month old like? I prefer toys that she has to engage or interact with." [sr023-0115]
- "i like the brand love every, but it’s incredibly expensive. i’m looking for toys of quality material, preferably wood, that are made to last a really long time & promote open ended play. i’m not opposed to plastic, eventually i’d like to get those magnetic tiles." [sr129-0116]
- "Hi all, my little boy is turning 1 next month. Are open ended toys worth it? I’m interested in buying him some grapat toys but idk where to start. Any advice and recommendations please? x" [sr099-0121]

**But:** Open-ended toys are still a question for one parent, rather than an established preference: "Are open ended toys worth it?" [sr099-0121]

