# baby-development: pattern 4, What should I get for this age?

**Written:** 2026-11-20 from baby-development/evidence/2026-11/second-reading/digest-10.md baby-development/evidence/2026-11/second-reading/digest-11.md
**Reviewed by the owner:** not yet

## Limits

A random, no-keyword sample covered 20,000 posts across twelve parenting subreddits, 1 April–24 October 2026; 2,471 were on-niche. This pattern contains 245 on-niche and 165 near posts; each count is posts tagged by one reader, not people or prevalence in the market. Forms named independently by digest readers were merged by judgement; cross-post tags overlap.

## On-niche posts

### They want gifts the child will use or keep.

31 of 245 posts.

They seek toys, experiences, practical gifts and keepsakes.

- \"small, easily stored, practical, consumable, or outdoors"'!" [sr025-0027]
- "a personalised gift that he can keep forever" [sr106-0033]

**But:** Some consider saving: "Saving the money as they’re too little to understand?" [sr131-0070]

### They need safe space as the child becomes mobile.

21 of 245 posts.

They seek mats, barriers and locks.

- "figured out how to open his door" [sr094-0101]
- "almost our entire living room" [sr128-0081]

**But:** Some need no containment yet: "haven'"'t really had issues yet.\" [sr046-0108]

### They need feeding equipment the child can use comfortably.

20 of 245 posts.

They compare cups, utensils and seating.

- \"it has 7 different parts"'!" [sr006-0096]
- "a good, reachable footrest for good posture." [sr069-0013]

**But:** Some skills already work: "LO drinks water great out of straws." [sr067-0043]

### They want books and learning resources suited to this stage.

20 of 245 posts.

They seek developmental value and parenting guidance.

- "is it better to prioritize visual contrast" [sr035-0096]
- "I read all the pregnancy and infant books" [sr060-0023]

**But:** More can hinder engagement: "he actually does better when he has less options" [sr121-0078]

### They need shoes that fit and allow comfortable movement.

18 of 245 posts.

They weigh grip, fit, weather and development.

- "I cannot get his feet in any shoe" [sr073-0106]
- "size 4 and huge on her." [sr083-0089]

**But:** Soft soles are not always best: "shoes with a harder sole which work a little bit better actually" [sr002-0248]

### They want toys matched to what their child enjoys.

14 of 245 posts.

Grabbing, chewing, movement and boredom shape requests.

- "What toys do I need for next month?" [sr068-0146]
- "advanced with fine motor so he gets bored" [sr099-0076]

**But:** Current play can delight: "a fishing style game which we both love" [sr027-0200]

### They ask when to change the sleep space.

14 of 245 posts.

They weigh containment, lifting and spending.

- "We just don’t want to spend unnecessary money" [sr005-0188]
- "Plus bending over the crib is a pain." [sr128-0127]

**But:** Some see no immediate need: "She hasn’t tried climbing out of it yet" [sr051-0123]

### They want safe items satisfying chewing and sensory interests.

14 of 245 posts.

They seek teethers, pacifiers, wire substitutes and screen-free stimulation.

- "satiate his appetite for delicious human flesh?" [sr002-0123]
- "**screen-free and battery-free**" [sr128-0092]

**But:** Pacifiers divide them: "your baby DOESNT need one." [sr105-0084]

### They want movement equipment that fits now and lasts.

13 of 245 posts.

Ability, space and price constrain choices.

- "Should I wait until he'"'s cruising?\" [sr107-0098]
- \"nervous spending "'$3-4K" [sr093-0104]

**But:** Some buy ahead: "this feature would not be used to closer to three" [sr096-0003]

### They need seats the baby can safely use and tolerate.

12 of 245 posts.

Sitting, weight and bath behaviour change needs.

- "Is it too early" [sr042-0002]
- "pee without a baby crying in the background." [sr030-0006]

**But:** Waiting is also considered: "It seems too early now to utilize" [sr068-0001]

### They need outing equipment that fits their growing child.

11 of 245 posts.

Requests cover transport and entertainment.

- "only about 42cm and most helmets start at 48cm" [sr046-0056]
- "Is she too little for that??" [sr050-0010]

**But:** Price need not decide: "Price isn’t a huge hurdle" [sr053-0139]

### They ask whether audio players and stories suit this child.

9 of 245 posts.

They weigh independence, content and readiness.

- "He’s really only interested in the songs!" [sr044-0037]
- "at what age would you introduce your son to Star Wars?" [sr097-0010]

**But:** Existing equipment may suffice: "from my phone or a speaker?" [sr085-0020]

### They want equipment letting the child join everyday routines.

8 of 245 posts.

Towers, potty arrangements and storage must fit safely.

- "a more accessible way for her to throw things away herself?" [sr011-0130]
- "she’s sooo tiny and can’t use regular toddler chairs." [sr093-0046]

**But:** Potty access need not mean training: "Not potty training, just potty exploring" [sr093-0046]

### They want clothing and swim gear fitting changing bodies.

8 of 245 posts.

Nappies, seasons, movement and water use matter.

- "I’m not one for fashion over function" [sr068-0025]
- "life vest I was expecting her to fit into by now is massive." [sr042-0030]

**But:** Some clothing already works: "Burt’s bees pajamas that work well" [sr085-0022]

### They question whether another purchase will be worth it.

7 of 245 posts.

They weigh usefulness, clutter and ignored purchases.

- "am I condemning myself to super 52 pick up??" [sr052-0122]
- "could have saved the money lol" [sr118-0050]

**But:** Some gear earns reuse: "I’d probably use a swing again" [sr118-0067]

### They want rooms supporting play and growing independence.

7 of 245 posts.

They plan accessible furniture and supervision.

- "had some delays due to a brain condition" [sr094-0069]
- "a small basket of toys to play by themselves" [sr068-0044]

**But:** Independence also worries them: "I'"'m a bit wary of letting them do too much by themselves\" [sr068-0042]

### They seek open-ended toys for active and imaginative play.

4 of 245 posts.

They favour engagement over lights.

- \"toys that she has to engage or interact with.\" [sr023-0115]
- \"it’s incredibly expensive.\" [sr129-0116]

**But:** Some remain undecided: \"Are open ended toys worth it?\" [sr099-0121]

### They need toys when activity or caregiving is limited.

4 of 245 posts.

Bed rest, birth, surgery and flights prompt requests.

- \"without requiring me to be mobile.\" [sr129-0072]
- \"sit on the couch and play with?\" [sr132-0043]

**But:** Travel plans also include ordinary objects: \"my bag contents and the airplane.\" [sr029-0013]

### They need car seats fitting growth and the next stage.

4 of 245 posts.

Fit, longevity and direction concern them.

- \"we obviously want this to last a while.\" [sr014-0111]
- \"I’m bummed bc I thought we’d get so much more use\" [sr131-0032]

**But:** Changing direction also frightens them: \"I am SCARED to switch him yet\" [sr100-0047]

### They question when standing or walking calls for shoes.

4 of 245 posts.

Outside pressure competes with barefoot preferences.

- \"shoes or else he will get flat feet?\" [sr049-0049]
- \"daycare said they need shoes once they start pulling up.\" [sr060-0040]

**But:** Some resist support: \"I feel like he should be free\" [sr002-0170]

### They want flotation allowing swimming practice.

2 of 245 posts.

They seek fit and swimming freedom.

- \"within that weight limit, any suggestions???\" [sr043-0058]
- \"work on his rolling from front to back\" [sr002-0005]

**But:** Supervision remains part of the request: \"We are always with him\" [sr002-0004]

## Near posts

### They need sleep spaces keeping up with growth and mobility.

35 of 165 posts.

They weigh bassinet limits, escape, transfers and preserving sleep.

- \"move out of the crib so early"'!!" [sr110-0058]
- "because it’s so deep" [sr037-0053]

**But:** Some seek independence despite calm waking: "she calmly talks to herself" [sr056-0099]

### They need protection as children defeat existing barriers.

25 of 165 posts.

Fittings complicate gates and locks.

- "a standard baby gate does not fit properly" [sr004-0074]
- "just left behind residue." [sr017-0234]

**But:** Removal sacrifices needed storage: "We don’t have enough extra storage elsewhere" [sr027-0124]

### They want resources teaching useful skills without unwanted content.

21 of 165 posts.

They seek books, apps, games and shows.

- "will actually help him learn to read" [sr030-0024]
- "rather than just getting free, easy stimulation" [sr100-0039]

**But:** Buying is optional: "making my own cards, so no biggie." [sr132-0070]

### They need sleepwear accommodating rolling, standing or escaping.

19 of 165 posts.

They fear losing sleep during changes.

- "I don'"'t want to mess that up.\" [sr023-0120]
- \"zipping herself out of her (backwards even) sleep sack.\" [sr038-0121]

**But:** Movement need not be rolling: \"The thing is she cannot roll\" [sr059-0001]

### They want practical transport and entertainment for outings.

14 of 165 posts.

Posture, disability, siblings and travel logistics shape requests.

- \"she has a moderate form of cerebral palsy\" [sr010-0083]
- \"My husband cannot come on the trip\" [sr076-0017]

**But:** Some found a solution: \"which has been great.\" [sr018-0054]

### They want clothing and swim gear permitting comfortable movement.

12 of 165 posts.

Fit, leaks, seasons and social expectations affect choices.

- \"it’s getting in his way as he rolls around\" [sr134-0025]
- \"Am I supposed to put pants on her in public?\" [sr004-0069]

**But:** Existing clothes can help: \"They help her do tummy time and practice rolling.\" [sr004-0068]

### They want feeding equipment supporting self-drinking and outings.

6 of 165 posts.

Milk acceptance, cleaning and portable seating matter.

- \"I bought three different straw cups already\" [sr022-0094]
- \"too small for the high chairs at the restaurant\" [sr053-0041]

**But:** The drink can be the obstacle: \"My baby already drinks water\" [sr022-0094]

### They need car seats suiting bodies, readiness and daily use.

4 of 165 posts.

Posture, cleaning and rear-facing longevity matter.

- \"pee has saturated every crevice of the base\" [sr005-0099]
- \"Is there a point developmentally where it’s safer?\" [sr039-0095]

**But:** Size alone does not persuade: \"We will not be doing that. She’s not even 4.\" [sr039-0095]

### They ask whether music equipment will suit their child.

3 of 165 posts.

Requests include instruments, independence and hearing or speech needs.

- \"just trendy or actually revolutionary.\" [sr011-0062]
- \"She has cochlear implants also.\" [sr082-0041]

**But:** Standard nursery content may miss the interest: \"She isn't interested in the typical nursery rhymes\" [sr016-0030]

### They struggle to find shoes fitting and protecting feet.

3 of 165 posts.

Development, sizing and spending concern them.

- \"I am broke as shit.\" [sr078-0040]
- \"bad for foot development, which i didnt even consider"'!!!" [sr029-0111]

**But:** Wide toes leave other worries: "he currently wears wide toed shoes" [sr029-0113]

### They want cushioning and bedding without compromising sleep safety.

3 of 165 posts.

Bumps, covered faces and restricted movement worry them.

- "a quilt of the same thickness under the sheet?" [sr024-0003]
- "hands and feet stuck between the slats" [sr099-0152]

**But:** One reports professional approval: "approved of our sleeping arrangements." [sr061-0070]

### They want toys reflecting real interests and activities.

3 of 165 posts.

They describe science, violin imitation and copying adults.

- "STEM toys either feel too school-like" [sr014-0229]
- "She’s MUCH more interested in what I’m doing." [sr048-0026]

**But:** Some current play works: "my kids love it honestly" [sr014-0231]

### They want fewer stored toys without losing useful play.

3 of 165 posts.

They weigh rotation, hand-me-downs, rewards and pretend play.

- "We are overrun with Hot Wheels." [sr025-0097]
- "I don’t want to curb imagination." [sr099-0081]

**But:** Keeping toys saves purchases: "we haven’t needed to purchase new toys for baby." [sr044-0018]

### They want lasting toys extending imaginative play.

2 of 165 posts.

Adults want to enjoy play too.

- "toys for imaginative and open ended play!" [sr080-0107]
- "What toys did you love" [sr084-0132]

**But:** Current toys already appeal: "My daughter is really into little people sets," [sr080-0107]

### They want active-play equipment fitting safely in their space.

2 of 165 posts.

Trampoline alternatives and playset adaptations expose safety constraints.

- "Is an airtrack suitable for jumping on" [sr098-0090]
- "I should have built in more space." [sr030-0083]

**But:** The work can feel worthwhile: "I'"'m glad I did it\" [sr030-0089]

### They need equipment for helping and toileting beyond home setups.

2 of 165 posts.

They seek cleaning and portable-toileting equipment.

- \"My toddler loves helping and cleaning.\" [sr027-0104]
- \"The toilets are too big for her to sit on\" [sr090-0062]

**But:** Some tasks still engage: \"He does love to wipe.\" [sr027-0105]

### They question whether introducing a comfort object will help.

1 of 165 posts.

Age is unknown; attachment and backups concern them.

- \"sleeping with or getting comfort from one?\" [sr024-0260]
- \"When/did you introduce them? Any regrets?\" [sr024-0262]

**But:** The child may choose differently: \"adopting a plastic colander or something instead\" [sr024-0263]

### They want a swim vest permitting arm movement.

1 of 165 posts.

One Canadian seeks approval; age is unknown.

- \"encourage her to swim using her arms.\" [sr096-0005]
- \"Preferrably Transport Canada or Canadian Coast Guard approved.\" [sr096-0006]

**But:** nothing found against it.

### They question buying equipment for a short remaining stage.

1 of 165 posts.

One mistook a sterilizer for a washer.

- \"actually thinking it was a bottle washer.\" [sr093-0068]
- \"not sure if it’s worth it\" [sr093-0068]

**But:** The appliance has another use: \"I also put my pump parts through the sterilizer\" [sr093-0068]

### Other requests concern removing adaptations, comfort, stimulation and design.

5 of 165 posts.

They include knee pads, commute toys and colours; a creator’s aphantasia-book concept is promotion or feedback, not an independent buyer report.

- \"Now she’s older and more coordinated I’m trying to get it off.\" [sr053-0096]
- \"Why is everything for babies grey, black, or beige?\" [sr087-0136]
- \"would a book like this help them to segue into graphic novels?\" [sr068-0128]

**But:** nothing found against it.

## Across the on-niche posts

### They have tested gear, adaptations and ordinary alternatives.

185 of 245 posts.

Attempts include secondhand searches, practice and household changes.

- \"We have tried those cooling gels and tablets\" [sr002-0125]
- \"pulling the lid out with the straw and spilling water everywhere.\" [sr027-0167]

**But:** Some trials succeed: \"handled the night like a champ.\" [sr128-0127]

### Other people influence what they acquire and when.

63 of 245 posts.

Family, daycare, professionals and ads influence choices.

- \"they’ve asked us to bring in stronger ones.\" [sr128-0123]
- \"I been getting ads for Lovevery, Kiwico and some others.\" [sr034-0057]

**But:** Influence need not produce agreement: \"My partner and I can't agree\" [sr125-0045]

### They report buying toys and practical developmental gear.

21 of 245 posts.

Purchases range from secondhand bargains to unsuccessful preparations.

- \"at a flea market today for "'$40." [sr012-0123]
- "I bought teethers early because I thought I was being prepared. Lol nope." [sr037-0031]

**But:** Purchases do not ensure use: "things that I’ve never used again for baby 🥲" [sr004-0134]

### They express overwhelm, worry and frustration about choosing gear.

58 of 245 posts.

They also describe guilt, disappointment, pride and excitement.

- "there’s so much and I feel overwhelmed lol" [sr008-0004]
- "Feeling very confused with all the recommendations and options" [sr070-0041]

**But:** Feelings also include joy: "my baby is finally getting a nursery (I am ecstatic lol)" [sr009-0056]

